INT. LOCKER ROOM - HALFTIME

Sweat, steam, rattling lockers. A whiteboard scrawled with arrows.

COACH MARGUERITE "MAGS" ODUYA-LINDGREN, 50s, paces with a clipboard. The team captain, JASMINE "JAZZ" ABERNATHY-OKORO, 20s, sits on a bench with a towel over her head.

COACH
Fourteen down.

JAZZ
I know.

COACH
Fourteen.

JAZZ
I know, Coach.

COACH
She knows, she says.

JAZZ
We know.

The coach slams the clipboard against a locker. Jazz flinches. She pulls the towel off, wipes her face, and doesn't look up.

COACH (CONT'D)
They run the same play every time. Every single time.

JAZZ
So why can't we stop it?

COACH
Because you're watching the ball.

JAZZ
We're supposed to watch the ball!

COACH
You're supposed to watch the hips!

The door bangs. A rookie stands there, sweating. DESHAWN "DEE" KOWALCZYK, 19, number twelve, helmet under her arm.

DEE
Coach. Can I say something?

COACH
No.

JAZZ
Yes.

DEE
I see it. The tell. The left shoulder drops before the screen.

Silence. The coach turns. Jazz lifts her chin.

COACH
Say that again.

DEE
Left shoulder. Every time.

JAZZ
(standing)
Then we hit it.

COACH
Then we hit it.
